  30,
  false,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free, but you need a free Alabama Hills camping permit (online, at the Eastern Sierra Visitor Center in Lone Pine, or at the Movie Road kiosks). The permit does not hold a site. About 50 signed sites, first come, first served. No water. Weekends fill up; nearby Tuttle Creek and Lone Pine campgrounds are backups.',
  array['Porta-potties at Mobius Arch trailhead and across from Shark Fin parking']::text[],
  array['Camp only in sites marked with a tent symbol. Everywhere else is day use only.', 'Free Alabama Hills camping permit required (good for one year)', 'Pack out solid human waste and toilet paper (wag bag or portable toilet) unless you use the porta-potties', 'Fires only in existing rings at designated sites, with a free California campfire permit. Check fire restrictions.', 'Stay up to 14 days per calendar year in the Bishop BLM Field Office area', 'Keep tents, vehicles and kitchens on bare ground. Don''t crush the brush.']::text[],
  'From US-395 in Lone Pine, turn west at the stoplight onto Whitney Portal Road. Drive 2.5 miles and turn right onto Movie Road. Look for signed sites with a tent symbol and check the map at the kiosk. The west side of Movie Road in the Movie Flat area is day use only. The map pin is approximate.',
  '(760) 872-5000',
  '[{"label":"BLM: Alabama Hills","url":"https://www.blm.gov/alabamahills"},{"label":"BLM: Alabama Hills National Scenic Area","url":"https://www.blm.gov/programs/national-conservation-lands/california/alabama-hills-national-scenic-area"},{"label":"Sierra Forever: Camping in the Alabama Hills","url":"https://sierraforever.org/?p=11439"},{"label":"Campendium: Movie Road Designated Dispersed Camping","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/lone-pine-ca/camping-rv/movie-road-designated-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"The Dyrt: Alabama Hills on Movie Flat Road","url":"https://www.thedyrt.com/camping/california/alabama-hills-on-movie-flat-road"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
