  'valley-of-the-gods',
  'Valley of the Gods near Bluff',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-109.81518, 37.2362), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'BLM · Monticello Field Office (Bears Ears National Monument)',
  14,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Graded gravel and clay loop (County Road 242) with sharp turns, rocky bits and several wash crossings. Fine for cars when dry. Spur roads to sites off the loop need high clearance.',
  true,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  25,
  null,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free. No water, toilets or trash service. Bring plenty of water. Cell service is spotty.',
  '{}'::text[],
  array['No campfires anywhere in Valley of the Gods', 'Camp only in already-used sites, away from ponds, corrals and archaeological sites', 'Pack out all trash and toilet paper', 'Keep pets out of archaeological sites', 'Stay up to 14 days in any 28-day period (BLM general limit)']::text[],
  'From US-163, about 15 miles west of Bluff and 7 miles east of Mexican Hat, turn north onto Valley of the Gods Road (County Road 242). Sites start near this east entrance. Towing the full 17-mile loop is not advised. The Moki Dugway on UT-261 is an 11% grade; take care with RVs and trailers.',
  '(435) 587-1500',
  '[{"label":"BLM: Valley of the Gods","url":"https://www.blm.gov/visit/search-details/269135/1"},{"label":"BLM: Valley of the Gods brochure (PDF)","url":"https://www.blm.gov/sites/blm.gov/files/documents/files/Utah_BENM_Valley-Of_Gods_Brochure.pdf"},{"label":"The Dyrt: Valley of the Gods Road Dispersed","url":"https://www.thedyrt.com/camping/utah/valley-of-the-gods-ut-2"},{"label":"Visit Bluff: Valley of the Gods","url":"https://bluffutah.org/valley-of-the-gods/"},{"label":"BLM: Camping on public lands","url":"https://blm.gov/programs/recreation/camping?page=1"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
  'hurricane-cliffs-sheep-bridge',
  'Hurricane Cliffs designated sites 1-12 (Sheep Bridge Road)',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-113.25235, 37.1632), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'BLM · St. George Field Office',
  14,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Unimproved dirt with washboard. Decent clearance helps. Wet silt and clay gets very slick.',
  true,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  35,
  null,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free. 56 numbered sites across the Hurricane Cliffs area, first come, first served; this pin is the group of sites 1-12. Most are taken by mid-afternoon on Fridays. Restrooms at the Sheep Bridge, JEM and Virgin Dam trailheads.',
  array['Metal fire ring at each site', 'Restrooms at nearby trailheads']::text[],
  array['Camp only at the numbered designated sites', 'Stay up to 14 days in any 28-day period', 'Fires only in the steel fire rings. Follow current fire restrictions.', 'Use the trailhead restrooms or bring a portable toilet', 'Turn around if your tires are leaving ruts in wet weather', 'Respect private property']::text[],
  'East of Hurricane on UT-59. Coming from Hurricane, Sheep Bridge Road is on the left just after you crest the hill, so get in the passing lane. Sites 2-12 are along Sheep Bridge Road; look for the numbered posts.',
  '(435) 688-3200',
  '[{"label":"BLM: Hurricane Cliffs Designated Dispersed Camping Area","url":"https://www.blm.gov/visit/hurricane-cliffs-designated-dispersed-camping-area"},{"label":"Campendium: Hurricane Cliffs Designated Dispersed Campsites 1-12","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/hurricane-ut/nature/hurricane-cliffs-designated-dispersed-campsites-1-12"},{"label":"St. George News: new camping plan between Hurricane and Zion (Apr 2026)","url":"https://www.stgeorgeutah.com/life/visitors-may-soon-find-new-places-to-camp-between-hurricane-and-zion-national-park/article_a3a6268b-5116-473f-92bc-03b481db5a41.html"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
