  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping with Sawtooth views. No facilities: no water, toilets or trash service. Get water in Stanley. Busy with ATVs on weekends.',
  array['Views of the Sawtooth Mountains', 'Close to Stanley and Redfish Lake']::text[],
  array['Stay up to 10 days in any 30 days from May 1 to Sept. 15, and 16 days the rest of the year. Confirm with the Stanley office', 'Store all food, scented items and trash in a closed hard-sided vehicle or trailer. Pickup beds and coolers do not count', 'Check current fire restrictions before any campfire. Some sites have fire rings', 'Pack out all trash']::text[],
  'Come in from the west end, off ID-21 on the northwest side of Stanley, and cross the bridge onto Nip and Tuck Road (FR 653). The best sites are 2.5 to 3 miles in. Big rigs should stay on the lower sections near ID-21. Avoid the east end from ID-75 in Lower Stanley: it has a deep, narrow wash.',
