  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free numbered sites, first come, first served. No water, toilets or trash service. Bear-proof trash bins are in West Yellowstone. Arrive early in summer.',
  array['Close to Yellowstone’s West Entrance and Hebgen Lake']::text[],
  array['Camp only at the numbered sites. Signs say no camping past site 4', 'Grizzly country: store food, trash and scented items in a hard-sided vehicle or bear-resistant container (March 1 to Dec. 1)', 'Stay up to 16 days in a row at one site and 32 days a year in all on Montana national forests', 'Check current fire restrictions before any campfire', 'Pack out all trash']::text[],
  'From West Yellowstone, drive about 7 to 8 miles west on US-20 and turn north on Denny Creek Road. The sites are on West Denny Creek Road (FR 1735). A camper says to stay right at each fork with the creek on your right; site 1 is on the left just before the creek crossing and the others are past it. The left fork ends at a locked gate.',
  '(406) 823-6961',
  '[{"label":"Campendium: West Fork Denny Creek Dispersed Camping","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/west-yellowstone-mt/camping-rv/west-fork-denny-creek-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"Forest Service: Custer Gallatin visitor information (May 2026)","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/media/268345"},{"label":"Forest Service: Northern Region camping stay limits (R1-2025-01)","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r01/alerts/r1-2025-01-camping-stay-limits-prohibitions-pallets-and-refuse-use-target-shooting"},{"label":"Forest Service: Custer Gallatin food storage order","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r01/custergallatin/alerts/food-storage-order"},{"label":"Forest Service: Cherry Creek Campground (Hebgen Lake District)","url":"https://fs.usda.gov/r01/custergallatin/recreation/cherry-creek-campground"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
