  0
),
(
  'pine-ridge-fr-714a-chadron',
  'Pine Ridge Forest Road 714A near Chadron',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-103.03805, 42.70981), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Nebraska National Forest · Pine Ridge Ranger District',
  14,
  2,
  '2wd-ok',
  'About 1.5 miles of one-lane dirt along the ridge. Reported in good shape, but there are hidden ditches on both sides and few places to pass',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  26,
  false,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free camping, but you drive through Chadron State Park to get here, which needs a Nebraska park entry permit: $7.35/day with Nebraska plates or $14.35/day with other plates (2026). Water and a dump station are in the state park.',
  array['Black Hills Overlook views', 'Trailheads at both ends of the road', 'Chadron State Park nearby']::text[],
  array['Stay up to 14 days in a row, then leave for 14 days', 'Camp beside the road. Side spurs are closed to motor vehicles', 'Fire restrictions were posted for the Pine Ridge in fall 2026. Check before any campfire', 'Pack it in, pack it out. Bury human waste 6 inches deep and 100 feet from water']::text[],
  'Drive into Chadron State Park on US-385 near Chadron and head to its western edge, where Forest Road 714A climbs to the Black Hills Overlook trailhead. Only a few sites fit vehicles, so most campers park right along the road. Campers say Google Maps directions can fail here.',
  '(308) 432-0300',
  '[{"label":"Campendium: Pine Ridge Dispersed Camping","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/chadron-ne/camping-rv/pine-ridge-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"The Dyrt: review of FR 714A boondocking","url":"https://thedyrt.com/review/66307"},{"label":"Forest Service: Nebraska National Forest, Pine Ridge","url":"https://fs.usda.gov/r02/nebraska/recreation/nebraska-national-forest-pine-ridge-chadron"},{"label":"Guide to the Nebraska National Forests and Grassland","url":"https://discovernwnebraska.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/A-Guide-to-the-Nebraska-National-Forests-and-Grassland.pdf"},{"label":"Nebraska Game and Parks: permit pricing","url":"https://outdoornebraska.gov/permits/permit-pricing/"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
  'scoria-pit-medora',
  'Scoria Pit Dispersed Camping near Medora',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-103.58862, 46.94544), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Dakota Prairie Grasslands · Little Missouri National Grassland · Medora Ranger District',
  14,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Maintained gravel, then a steep, one-lane S-curve climb with blind spots to the upper sites (6 and up). Muddy at the entrance after rain',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  35,
  true,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free. About 14 to 20 numbered sites, first come, first served, and often full by mid-afternoon. No water, toilets or trash service. Fill water and dump in Medora.',
  array['Badlands views', 'Close to Theodore Roosevelt National Park and Medora']::text[],
  array['Camp only at the numbered sites. Don’t make new sites', 'Stay up to 14 days in a row and 28 days a year in all', 'Check Dakota Prairie Grasslands fire restrictions before any fire. Campers disagree on whether fires are allowed here', 'Stay away from oil and gas well sites, fenced or not', 'The area can close for special events. Check Forest Service alerts before you go']::text[],
  'A few miles northwest of Medora off West River Road, near I-94 Exit 23. Exit 23 has no westbound on-ramp, so go east to Exit 24 to turn around. Big rigs should take the lower sites and go slow on the hill.',
  '(701) 227-7800',
  '[{"label":"Campendium: Scoria Pit Dispersed Camping","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/medora-nd/camping-rv/scoria-pit-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"The Dyrt: Scoria Pit Dispersed Camping","url":"https://thedyrt.com/camping/north%20dakota/scoria-pit-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"Forest Service: Dispersed camping on the grasslands","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r01/dpg/recreation/dispersed-camping-grasslands"},{"label":"Forest Service: Northern Region camping stay limits (R1-2025-01)","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r01/alerts/r1-2025-01-camping-stay-limits-prohibitions-pallets-and-refuse-use-target-shooting"},{"label":"Forest Service: Medora Ranger District","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r01/dpg/offices/medora-ranger-district"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
  'pinnacles-nomad-view-wall',
