  'dispersed',
  'Buffalo Gap National Grassland · Wall Ranger District',
  14,
  2,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Gravel and dirt grassland roads, bumpy and dusty. Turns to slick mud in rain',
  true,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  null,
  null,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free. About 70 sites marked with wooden posts along the Badlands rim, first come, first served. Often full by late afternoon in summer. No water, toilets or trash. Use private dump stations nearby.',
  array['Badlands rim views', 'Close to Badlands National Park and Wall']::text[],
  array['Camp only at a numbered post, on the side of the road away from the rim', 'Stay up to 14 days', 'Keep off fenced restoration areas, and don’t camp in the day-use parking', 'Drive only on roads shown on the Motor Vehicle Use Map. Avoid driving when wet', 'Check fire restrictions at blackhillsfirerestrictions.com before any fire', 'Pets must be leashed or under voice control. Cattle graze here May to September']::text[],
  'About 6 miles south of Wall off SD-240. Take Forest Roads 7158 and 7170 to the numbered posts; campers say the turn is by the radio towers. High winds and storms come up fast, so stay back from the crumbly rim.',
  '(605) 279-2126',
  '[{"label":"Forest Service: Pinnacles Dispersed Camping Area","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r02/nebraska/recreation/pinnacles-dispersed-camping-area"},{"label":"Campendium: Nomad View Dispersed Camping","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/wall-sd/places/nomad-view-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"The Dyrt: Buffalo Gap Dispersed Camping (The Wall)","url":"https://thedyrt.com/camping/south-dakota/the-wall-dispersed-camping-just-outside-badlands"},{"label":"Black Hills Parks & Forests: Pinnacles restoration","url":"https://blackhillsparks.org/pinnacles-camping-restoration/"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
