  'shadow-mountain-jackson',
  'Shadow Mountain Designated Sites near Grand Teton',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-110.62616, 43.70004), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Bridger-Teton National Forest · Jackson Ranger District',
  5,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Paved to the camping area entrance, then rutted, rocky dirt. Low cars can reach the lower sites. The summit loop is rough and turns to mud in rain',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  null,
  false,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free. About 50 numbered sites, first come, first served, often full by late morning in summer. A sign at the turnoff shows when it’s full. Vault toilets at the base, no water.',
  array['Vault toilets at the base', 'Steel fire rings at most sites']::text[],
  array['Camp only at marked, numbered sites', 'Stay up to 5 days in any 30 days from May 1 to Labor Day', 'Grizzly and black bear country: store food and scented items in a hard-sided vehicle', 'Have at least 5 gallons of water and a shovel before you light a campfire', 'A camp ambassador patrols in summer']::text[],
  'From Jackson, take US-26/89 north 13.3 miles. Turn right on Antelope Flats Road, go 3.3 miles to the stop sign, and turn left to reach the camping area near Kelly. Lower sites fill first; the summit loop is rough.',
  '(307) 739-5400',
  '[{"label":"The Dyrt: Shadow Mountain Dispersed Camping","url":"https://thedyrt.com/camping/wyoming/shadow-mountain-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"Forest Service: Bridger-Teton camping","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r04/bridger-teton/recreation/camping-cabins"},{"label":"Forest Service: 5-day stay limit order","url":"https://fs.usda.gov/r04/bridger-teton/alerts/camping-5-day-stay-limit-jackson-blackrock-big-piney-greys-river-ranger"},{"label":"Visit Jackson Hole: Camping at Designated Sites","url":"https://visitjacksonhole.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Camping-at-Designated-Sites_trifold.pdf"},{"label":"Bridger-Teton Friends: camping guide","url":"https://www.btfriends.org/guides/camping"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
  'vedauwoo-fr-700',
  'Vedauwoo Designated Dispersed Sites (FR 700)',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-105.35393, 41.15538), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Medicine Bow National Forest · Laramie Ranger District (Pole Mountain area)',
  16,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Washboard gravel with ruts and potholes on the entry road. The spur roads are smoother',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  null,
  null,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free. 97 numbered sites with rock fire rings, first come, first served. No water or trash service. Busy on summer weekends; weekdays are easier.',
  array['Vault toilets at Nautilus Rock Trailhead and on FR 700D', 'Hiking trails, including the Turtle Rock loop', 'Beaver ponds']::text[],
  array['Camp only at numbered sites. Keep vehicles and fires within 50 feet of the site marker', 'Stay up to 16 days at a site', 'No more than 2 vehicles per site. Groups over 8 must use a group site', 'Pack out all trash and human and pet waste', 'Check Medicine Bow fire restrictions before any campfire', 'The road is closed to vehicles about February through May']::text[],
  'Take I-80 Exit 329 (Vedauwoo), about 16 miles east of Laramie or 30 miles west of Cheyenne. Take FR 700 (left from Laramie, right from Cheyenne) and drive about 2 miles east. It’s often windy, and cattle graze here.',
  '(307) 745-2300',
  '[{"label":"Forest Service: Vedauwoo Designated Dispersed Campsites","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r02/mbrtb/recreation/vedauwoo-designated-dispersed-campsites"},{"label":"The Dyrt: Forest Service Road 700 Designated Dispersed Camping","url":"https://thedyrt.com/camping/undefined/dispersed-camping-vedauwoo-road"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
  'forest-road-29-sappho',
  'Forest Road 29 near Sappho',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-124.11133, 48.04893), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Olympic National Forest · Pacific Ranger District',
  14,
  2,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Paved road in good shape to a gravel camping area. Farther up, FR 29 turns to gravel and gets narrower and rockier.',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  40,
  true,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No toilets, water or trash service. The main area fits about 10 RVs. If it is full, campers use a bigger gravel lot just past the next left.',
  '{}'::text[],
  array['Stay up to 14 days at one spot', 'A 2024–2026 forest order capped camping at 21 days per calendar year on Olympic National Forest. Check whether it has been renewed', 'Logging trucks use the road on weekdays. Keep the road clear', 'Pack out all trash', 'Check current fire restrictions before making a campfire']::text[],
  'From US 101 between Lake Crescent and Sappho, turn south on Cooper Ranch Road, which becomes Forest Road 29. The camping area is about a mile in. Handy for Sol Duc and Forks.',
  '(360) 374-6522',
