),
(
  'old-cascade-highway-skykomish',
  'Old Cascade Highway near Skykomish',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-121.20891, 47.71844), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest · Skykomish Ranger District',
  14,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Paved old highway with rocks sticking up in places and a big rock at the turn into one site. The site just south of the bridge is 4WD only.',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  0,
  false,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No toilets, water or trash service. Small sites, about nine near the bridge. Some riverside tent spots are a short walk from parking. Cell service is spotty, and the tall trees can block Starlink.',
  array['River access']::text[],
  array['Stay up to 14 days at one spot and 28 days per calendar year on the forest', 'Store food in a bear-resistant way (forest-wide food storage order)', 'Camp at least 100 feet from the river', 'Pack out all trash and toilet paper', 'Check fire restrictions before making a campfire']::text[],
  'From Skykomish, drive east on US 2 a few miles and turn onto the Old Cascade Highway. Sites are spread within about a mile on either side of a bridge. Campers say to watch for the turnoff on the right just before the bridge. Walk the turn-in first: a big rock sits at the entrance to one site.',
  '(360) 677-2414',
  '[{"label":"The Dyrt: Old Cascades Highway Dispersed","url":"https://www.thedyrt.com/camping/washington/old-cascades-highway-dispersed"},{"label":"Forest Service: Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie dispersed camping","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r06/mbs/recreation/dispersed-camping"},{"label":"Forest Service: Skykomish District road damage and closures (Old Cascade Highway not listed)","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r06/mbs/alerts/road-damages-closures-skykomish-district"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
