  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No toilets, water or trash service. Busy on summer weekends. The nearby Trillium Lake day-use area charges $10 per vehicle; campers report no fee at the airstrip.',
  array['Mount Hood views', 'Trillium Lake loop trail nearby']::text[],
  array['Stay up to 14 days at one spot and 28 days per calendar year on the forest', 'No camping along state or US highways, or in developed sites like trailheads and campgrounds', 'Pack out everything you bring. Campers ask everyone to keep it clean so the area stays open', 'Check fire restrictions before making a campfire']::text[],
  'From Government Camp, drive about 2 miles east on US 26. Turn right on Trillium Lake Road, then right on East Perry Vickers Road to the old airstrip. A gate across the road is closed under snow in winter and early spring.',
  '(503) 668-1700',
  '[{"label":"Campendium: Trillium Lake Airstrip","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/government-camp-or/nature/trillium-lake-airstrip"},{"label":"The Dyrt: dispersed camping near Government Camp (Mar 2026 review)","url":"https://thedyrt.com/camping/oregon/near/government-camp/with/dispersed"},{"label":"Islands: free dispersed camping in Mt. Hood National Forest (Apr 2026)","url":"https://www.islands.com/2141128/5-stunning-destinations-free-dispersed-camping-oregons-mt-hood-national-forest/"},{"label":"Forest Service: Mt. Hood dispersed camping","url":"https://fs.usda.gov/r06/mthood/recreation/dispersed-camping"},{"label":"Mountain Times: dispersed vs. designated camping on Mt. Hood","url":"https://mountaintimesoregon.com/2025/06/05/dispersed-vs-designated-camping-on-mt-hood"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
