  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Wide gravel road with washboard, potholes and lots of dust. Side spurs have loose sand that can trouble 2WD cars, and some need high clearance.',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  26,
  null,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No toilets, water or trash service. Many large, level, spread-out sites with stone fire rings in pine forest. Good Verizon and T-Mobile signal reported.',
  array['Mountain bike and hiking trails nearby']::text[],
  array['Deschutes NF Order 06-01-26-01 (2026–2031) bans camping in the Whychus Creek riparian corridor and a few other listed areas. Check the order before you pick a site', 'Campfires are often banned in summer. Check current fire restrictions', 'Stay up to 14 days', 'Pack out all trash']::text[],
  'From Sisters, take Three Creek Road south. Turn onto Forest Road 4606 (the Brooks Scanlon logging road) and keep going to find pull-offs and side spurs. The turnoff is hard to see in the dark. Mountain bikers sometimes ride past camps.',
  '(541) 383-5300',
  '[{"label":"The Dyrt: Sisters, Oregon Dispersed Camping","url":"https://thedyrt.com/camping/oregon/dispersed-camping-near-sisters"},{"label":"Forest Service: Deschutes camping and campfire restrictions (Order 06-01-26-01)","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r06/deschutes/alerts/camping-campfire-restrictions-forest-order"}]'::jsonb,
