(
  'alvord-desert-playa',
  'Alvord Desert Playa',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-118.53283, 42.55979), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'BLM · Burns District',
  14,
  2,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Long washboard gravel roads to a flat, dry lakebed. Sharp shale gravel is hard on tires. The playa clay turns slick and traps vehicles when wet.',
  true,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  25,
  null,
  true,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free. The only facility is a vault toilet at Frog Springs. No water, no shade and little or no cell service. Fuel and food are in Fields, about an hour south. Help is hours away: bring extra water and a spare tire.',
  array['Vault toilet at Frog Springs']::text[],
  array['Pack out everything, including human and pet waste', 'Don''t drive on the playa if it is wet or even looks damp', 'Weddings, races, vehicle rallies and large gatherings need a BLM permit', 'Check BLM fire restrictions. When fires are allowed, keep them in a raised fire pan', 'Winds are strong and sudden: tie everything down']::text[],
  'From Burns, take OR-78 southeast about 65 miles. Turn right (south) on East Steens Road (Folly Farm Road) and go about 40 miles southwest. Turn left (east) on the Frog Springs access road to reach the playa. The playa is usually dry enough to drive June through November.',
  '(541) 573-4400',
  '[{"label":"BLM: Alvord Desert playa","url":"https://www.blm.gov/visit/alvord-desert"},{"label":"Campendium: Alvord Desert","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/fields-or/nature/alvord-desert-or--4"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
  'sand-flat-mount-shasta',
  'Sand Flat on Mount Shasta',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-122.24969, 41.35393), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Shasta-Trinity National Forest · Mount Shasta Ranger District',
  14,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Dirt forest roads. The lower road is narrow but OK slowly in most vehicles. The upper loop has ruts, gullies and large rocks: high clearance recommended.',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  26,
  null,
  true,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No toilets, water or trash service. Sites spread along the forest roads, from full sun to shade, many with Mount Shasta views. Weekends fill up; weekdays are quieter.',
  array['Sand Flat Trailhead to Horse Camp']::text[],
  array['A free California Campfire Permit is required year-round for campfires and camp stoves on the forest', 'Stay up to 14 days in one spot and 30 days per calendar year on the forest', 'Camp at least 200 feet from water, meadows and trails', 'Hiking into the Mount Shasta Wilderness needs a wilderness permit. No dogs or wood fires there']::text[],
  'From Mount Shasta city, drive about 11 miles up Everitt Memorial Highway. About 0.8 mile below Bunny Flat, turn left onto the Sand Flat dirt road. Reviewers suggest the lower road for entry. Walk ahead to check spots before driving in with anything bigger than a van.',
  '(530) 926-4511',
  '[{"label":"Campendium: Sand Flat Dispersed Camping","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/mount-shasta-ca/nature/sand-flat-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"Forest Service: Mt. Shasta Wilderness access guide (Sand Flat Trailhead)","url":"https://fs.usda.gov/media/134728"},{"label":"Forest Service: Shasta-Trinity dispersed camping rules","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/sites/nfs/files/legacy-media/shasta-trinity/Dispersed%20Camping%20ROG.pdf"},{"label":"Forest Service: Shasta-Trinity current conditions","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r05/shasta-trinity/conditions"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
