  'north-manzanita-lassen',
  'North Manzanita Dispersed near Lassen Volcanic',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-121.59467, 40.53707), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Lassen National Forest',
  14,
  3,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Dusty dirt road with deep ruts in places. Fine for 2WD near the highway when dry. Rougher deeper in, where 4x4 helps.',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  23,
  null,
  true,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No toilets, water or trash service. A creek is about 100 yards up the road (treat the water). Highway 44 traffic is audible from the front sites. Weak or no cell service; Starlink works.',
  array['Creek nearby', 'Close to Manzanita Lake in Lassen Volcanic National Park']::text[],
  array['Stay no more than 14 days within a mile of one site, and 30 days a year outside campgrounds (2024–2026 forest order; check for renewal)', 'A free California Campfire Permit is needed for campfires and stoves outside campgrounds', 'Burn bans are common. If fires are allowed, sweep pine needles to bare dirt around the ring', 'Bears are active here. Keep food locked up', 'Pack out all trash']::text[],
  'Off Highway 44 near the northwest (Manzanita Lake) entrance of Lassen Volcanic National Park. Turn onto the gravel forest road; the first sites are on the first rise and in a clearing within about 100 yards of the highway. Quieter sites are farther up the road.',
  '(530) 257-2151',
  '[{"label":"The Dyrt: 31N17N - North Manzanita Dispersed Camping","url":"https://www.thedyrt.com/camping/california/31n17n-north-manzanita-dispersed-camping"},{"label":"Forest Service: Lassen National Forest camping restrictions (Order 06-24-01)","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/r05/lassen/alerts/forest-order-number-06-24-01-lassen-national-forest-camping-restrictions"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
  'hardin-flat-road-yosemite',
  'Hardin Flat Road near Yosemite',
  extensions.st_setsrid(extensions.st_makepoint(-119.9056, 37.81113), 4326)::extensions.geography,
  'dispersed',
  'Stanislaus National Forest · Groveland Ranger District',
  21,
  1,
  '2wd-ok',
  'Paved roads to the sites, per reviewers. In spring, snow, mud and fallen trees can block the upper ridge.',
  null,
  true,
  true,
  true,
  44,
  true,
  null,
  0,
  null,
  '{}'::text[],
  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No toilets, water or trash service. Only a handful of big sites, and they fill fast in peak season. About 3 miles from the Big Oak Flat entrance to Yosemite.',
  '{}'::text[],
  array['A free California Campfire Permit is required for campfires, stoves and lanterns outside campgrounds', 'Camp no more than 21 days per calendar year in a ranger district', 'Park within one vehicle length of the road. Camp at least 100 feet from meadows, lakes and streams', 'Forest roads close for winter from about December 15 to April 15', 'Check current fire restrictions before making a campfire']::text[],
  'Off CA 120 a few miles west of Yosemite''s Big Oak Flat entrance. Turn onto Hardin Flat Road (some campers come in on Golden Arrow Road) and look for sites along the forest roads. Hardin Flat Road also passes private resorts: camp only on national forest land.',
  '(209) 962-7825',
  '[{"label":"Campendium: Hardin Flat Road Dispersed Campsites","url":"https://maps.campendium.com/us/groveland-ca/camping-rv/hardin-flat-road-dispersed-campsites"},{"label":"Forest Service: Stanislaus dispersed camping guide (Aug 2026)","url":"https://www.fs.usda.gov/media/273067"}]'::jsonb,
  false,
  0
),
(
