  'not-needed',
  'Free dispersed camping. No water, toilets or trash service.',
  array['Lake Huron shoreline', 'Fire rings at many sites']::text[],
  array['Camp off the beach: Forest Service staff asked a camper on the beach to move (Aug 2025)', 'Hiawatha NF has allowed up to 16 days in a row at one spot; check with the district', 'Don''t leave gear unattended more than 24 hours', 'Park within 25 feet of the road', 'Pack out all trash, and never leave food scraps on the ground']::text[],
  'On the Lake Huron shore of Search Bay, just west of Hessel and about 13 miles from St. Ignace. A potholed two-track runs along the shore with sites on both sides. Sites near the entrance can take small RVs; past that, stick to vans, truck campers and small rigs (an 18 ft Class B with a kayak trailer was about the limit). Bring bug spray in late spring and early summer.',
