  'Free, first come, first served. 13 numbered sites with fire rings. No water, toilets or trash service.',
  array['Fire ring at each site', 'Gale River nearby', 'Hiking trails within walking distance']::text[],
  array['Camp only at the numbered sites. This road is in a Forest Protection Area', 'Follow the rules posted at each site (campers report 15 people and 3 cars per site)', 'Stay up to 14 days', 'Keep pets on a leash', 'Store food securely: campers have seen bears nearby', 'Pack it in, pack it out']::text[],
  'Off US 3 near Bethlehem, between Franconia Notch and Twin Mountain. Sites 1–3 are on the first part of the loop road, tent-only sites 4 and 5 are straight ahead at the crossing, and sites 6–13 are on the right branch. Big rigs should aim for site 3 and avoid dead-end side roads. Sites fill fast in summer and fall, so have a backup. Usually open about May through October; the gate can still be closed in mid-May.',
